You can do that today with PyScript:<p><pre><code>  &lt;script type=&quot;module&quot; src=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;pyscript.net&#x2F;releases&#x2F;2025.8.1&#x2F;core.js&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;script&gt;
  &lt;py-script&gt;
  import sys
  from pyscript import display
  display(sys.version)
  &lt;&#x2F;py-script&gt;
</code></pre>
Demo: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;static.simonwillison.net&#x2F;static&#x2F;2025&#x2F;pyscript-demo.html" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;static.simonwillison.net&#x2F;static&#x2F;2025&#x2F;pyscript-demo.h...</a><p>Or you can use MicroPython which is much smaller:<p><pre><code>    &lt;mpy-script&gt;
      import sys
      from pyscript import display
      display(sys.version)
    &lt;&#x2F;mpy-script&gt;
</code></pre>
